{"kind":"table","sheet":"COVER","address":"A1:D35","rows":35,"cols":4,"values":[[null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"NAVAL ARCHITECTURE",null,null],[null,"TEACHING TOOLKIT",null,null],[null,"An Open Educational Resource for Engineering Students",null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,null,"Alper Alaçam  |  Naval Architect & Marine Engineer  |  Türkiye  |  2026",null],[null,"ABOUT THIS WORKBOOK",null,null],[null,"What is this?","This free workbook introduces the fundamental calculations of Naval Architecture — the engineering discipline concerned with the design, construction and operation of ships, submarines and offshore structures. Every formula shown here is derived from established textbooks and international standards. Nothing is made up.",null],[null,"Who is it for?","Undergraduate naval architecture and marine engineering students, self-taught enthusiasts, and any engineer curious about how ships are designed. No prior knowledge of naval architecture is assumed — only basic algebra and a willingness to explore.",null],[null,"How to use it","Start with the VESSEL PARAMETERS sheet. Enter your ship dimensions there. Every other sheet will automatically update. Cells highlighted in GOLD with BLUE text are inputs you change. All other cells are formulas — do not edit them. Read the explanatory boxes on each sheet to understand WHY each calculation matters.",null],[null,"Units","This workbook uses SI units throughout: metres (m), tonnes (t = 1000 kg), kilonewtons (kN), and knots for speed. Seawater density = 1.025 t/m³. Freshwater density = 1.000 t/m³.",null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"WORKSHEET INDEX",null,null],[null,"No.","Sheet Name","Contents"],[null,"1","COVER","This page — introduction and guide"],[null,"2","VESSEL PARAMETERS","Master input sheet — enter your ship dimensions here"],[null,"3","HYDROSTATICS","Displacement, waterplane area, metacentric radii, BM, KB, GM"],[null,"4","RESISTANCE","Calm-water resistance, effective power, Froude number"],[null,"5","STABILITY","Initial stability, GZ righting levers, IMO criteria check"],[null,"6","WEIGHTS & TRIM","Lightweight, deadweight, KG estimation, trim and LCB balance"],[null,"7","FREEBOARD","Load line freeboard — simplified educational calculation"],[null,"8","SUBMARINE","Pressure hull, diving depth, reserve buoyancy (intro module)"],[null,"9","REFERENCE TABLES","Cb ranges, Froude numbers, GM limits, density table, coefficients"],[null,"10","CHARTS & GRAPHS","Auto-updating charts: speed-power curve, GZ curve, hydrostatics"],[null,null,null,null],[null,"COLOUR LEGEND",null,null],[null,"Blue text on gold background",null,"USER INPUT — change these cells"],[null,"Black text on white background",null,"FORMULA — do not edit"],[null,"Grey text on light blue",null,"EXPLANATION — educational notes"],[null,"Green text on green background",null,"RESULT PASSES check / within limits"],[null,"Red text on red background",null,"RESULT FAILS check / outside limits"],[null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"© 2025 Alper Alacam Naval Architecture — Concept Design Studio  |  All rights reserved. Knowledge must be free — share this workbook freely with students and educators.",null,null]]}
