{"kind":"table","sheet":"COVER","address":"A1:D30","rows":30,"cols":4,"values":[[null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"NAVAL ARCHITECTURE",null,null],[null,"TEACHING TOOLKIT",null,null],[null,"VOLUME 17 :  Bow Design",null,null],[null,"Hydrodynamics, Structure, Special Forms and Anchor Equipment",null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"Alper Alacam  |  Naval Architect and Marine Engineer  |  Turkiye  |  2026",null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"ABOUT THIS VOLUME",null,null],[null,"The engineering challenge","The bow is the most complex and consequential part of a ship. It must simultaneously minimise wave-making resistance, survive green water and slamming impacts, provide adequate freeboard, house the anchor and mooring equipment, and in some cases break ice or pierce waves in extreme sea states. Every previous volume treated the ship as a body of known geometry. This volume asks: how do you design that geometry at the forward end? What angle should the stem make? Should there be a bulbous bow? What structural scantlings resist slamming pressure? What is the correct anchor weight?",null],[null,"Connection to earlier volumes","Vol.1: ship form coefficients Cp and Cwp govern bow geometry. Vol.2: wave-making resistance theory explains why bulbous bows work. Vol.4: structural scantling method applied to bow plating and stem bar. Vol.12: Holtrop-Mennen A_BT and C_1 inputs come from this volume's bulb design. Vol.13: slamming probability and relative bow motion from seakeeping analysis. Vol.14: anchor chain MBL formula uses same IACS chain standard.",null],[null,"What this volume covers","Bow geometry parameters: entry angle, stem profile, flare, forefoot. Bulbous bow design using the Kracht (1978) SNAME method: C_BB, C_BL, C_BT, C_BV, C_BPo parameters, bulb type classification. Resistance reduction calculation from bulb geometry. Slamming pressure from Ochi and Motter (1973) and Faltinsen (1990). Green water assessment. Bow structural scantlings per DNV Rules. Collision bulkhead position per SOLAS Chapter II-1 Regulation 11. Special bow forms: X-bow, axe bow, wave-piercing, icebreaking. Anchor and mooring equipment from IACS UR A1 (2019). Bow design philosophy by ship type.",null],[null,"Primary references","Kracht A.M. (1978) Design of bulbous bows. SNAME Transactions 86:197-217. Inui T. (1962) Wavemaking resistance of ships. SNAME Transactions 70:283-353. Faltinsen O.M. (1990) Sea Loads on Ships and Offshore Structures. Cambridge UP. Ochi M.K. and Motter L.E. (1973) Prediction of slamming characteristics. SNAME Transactions 81:144-176. SOLAS (2020) Chapter II-1 Part B Regulation 11. IACS UR A1 (2019) Anchoring Equipment. IACS. IACS UR W22 (2019) Stud link chain cables. IACS. DNV Rules for Classification (2022) Part 3 Chapter 10.",null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"WORKSHEET INDEX",null,null],[null,"No.","Sheet","Contents"],[null,"1","COVER","Introduction, connections to earlier volumes, references"],[null,"2","BOW GEOMETRY","Entry angle, stem profile, flare, forefoot, knuckle lines"],[null,"3","BULBOUS BOW","Kracht (1978) method: C_BB, C_BL, C_BT, C_BV, C_BPo, bulb types"],[null,"4","BULB RESISTANCE","Bulb dimensions, A_BT, V_B, resistance reduction calculation"],[null,"5","SLAMMING","Ochi-Motter slamming pressure, green water, flare impact"],[null,"6","BOW STRUCTURE","SOLAS collision bulkhead, plating, stem bar, DNV scantlings"],[null,"7","SPECIAL BOW FORMS","X-bow, axe bow, wave-piercing, icebreaking, Maierform"],[null,"8","ANCHOR EQUIPMENT","IACS UR A1 equipment number, anchor mass, chain, windlass"],[null,"9","BOW BY SHIP TYPE","Container, tanker, bulk carrier, LNG, RoPax, OSV, naval"],[null,"10","REFERENCE TABLES","Kracht parameters, entry angle vs Cp, Cs coefficients, charts"],[null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"© 2026 Alper Alacam Naval Architecture . All rights reserved.",null,null]]}
{"kind":"table","sheet":"BOW GEOMETRY","address":"A1:E37","rows":37,"cols":5,"values":[[null,null,null,null,null],[null,"BOW GEOMETRY AND PARAMETERS -- DEFINING THE FORWARD HULL FORM",null,null,null],[null,"Before designing the details of the bow, the overall geometric parameters mus...",null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,"SHIP PRINCIPAL DIMENSIONS INPUTS",null,null,null]],"valuesTruncated":true,"valuesPreviewRows":5,"valuesPreviewCols":5,"valuesPreviewAddress":"A1:E5"}
