{"kind":"table","sheet":"COVER","address":"A1:D31","rows":31,"cols":4,"values":[[null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"NAVAL ARCHITECTURE",null,null],[null,"TEACHING TOOLKIT",null,null],[null,"VOLUME 18 :  Gas and Steam Turbines",null,null],[null,"Thermodynamics, Aerodynamics, Metallurgy and Blade Manufacturing",null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"Alper Alacam  |  Naval Architect and Marine Engineer  |  Turkiye  |  2026",null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"ABOUT THIS VOLUME",null,null],[null,"The engineering masterpiece","The gas turbine blade is arguably the single most sophisticated manufactured object in human history. It operates at temperatures exceeding its own melting point, cooled internally by air through hundreds of tiny holes. It spins at 10,000 to 20,000 rpm under centrifugal stresses of 100,000 g. It survives thermal cycling from cold start to full power in minutes and must do this for 25,000 hours without failure. The progression from equiaxed casting to directional solidification to single crystal growth via the Bridgman process is one of the greatest materials achievements of the 20th century.",null],[null,"What this volume covers","Brayton cycle gas turbine thermodynamics: compressor work, turbine work, thermal efficiency, regeneration, combined cycle. Rankine cycle steam turbine thermodynamics: pump work, boiler heat, turbine work, specific steam consumption, reheat cycle, marine LNG carrier steam plant. Turbomachinery aerodynamics: Euler equation, velocity triangles, stage loading, degree of reaction, Smith (1965) efficiency, Zweifel blade loading coefficient. Nickel superalloy metallurgy: gamma-prime precipitate, creep, Larson-Miller parameter, hot corrosion, alloy evolution from Nimonic 80A to CMSX-10. Blade casting: investment casting, Bridgman process, directional solidification, single crystal growth, spiral grain selector, G/R ratio stability criterion. Thermal barrier coatings: MCrAlY bond coat, 7YSZ top coat, temperature drop calculation. Marine gas turbines: LM2500, MT30, COGAG, CODAG, COGES, NOx limits. Performance calculations: full Brayton and Rankine cycle calculators.",null],[null,"Trade secret boundary","The Bridgman process and single crystal growth physics are fully covered from open literature. What this volume does NOT include: specific cooling channel geometry of any production blade, exact alloy compositions beyond published general ranges, specific directional solidification withdrawal rates of any manufacturer, proprietary heat treatment schedules. These are legitimately protected trade secrets. The open literature is more than sufficient to understand the physics completely.",null],[null,"Primary references","Dixon S.L. and Hall C.A. (2014) Fluid Mechanics and Thermodynamics of Turbomachinery 7th ed. Butterworth-Heinemann. Reed R.C. (2006) The Superalloys: Fundamentals and Applications. Cambridge UP. Bridgman P.W. (1925) Proc American Academy Arts Sciences 60:305-383. Versnyder F.L. and Shank M.E. (1970) Mat Sci Eng 6:213-247. Larson F.R. and Miller J. (1952) Trans ASME 74:765-771. Smith S.F. (1965) J Royal Aeronautical Society 69:467-470. Rolls-Royce plc (1996) The Jet Engine 5th ed. Boyce M.P. (2012) Gas Turbine Engineering Handbook 4th ed.",null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"WORKSHEET INDEX",null,null],[null,"No.","Sheet","Contents"],[null,"1","COVER","Introduction, trade secret boundary, references"],[null,"2","GAS TURBINE THERMO","Brayton cycle, compressor work, turbine work, efficiency, regeneration"],[null,"3","STEAM TURBINE THERMO","Rankine cycle, pump, boiler, turbine, SSC, reheat, LNG carrier plant"],[null,"4","TURBOMACHINERY AERO","Euler equation, velocity triangles, psi, phi, reaction, Smith chart"],[null,"5","BLADE MATERIALS","Nickel superalloys, gamma-prime, creep, Larson-Miller, hot corrosion"],[null,"6","BLADE CASTING","Bridgman process, DS, single crystal, spiral selector, G/R ratio"],[null,"7","COATINGS AND COOLING","MCrAlY bond coat, 7YSZ TBC, film cooling, temperature drop"],[null,"8","MARINE GAS TURBINES","LM2500, MT30, COGAG, CODAG, COGES, NOx, inlet filtration"],[null,"9","STEAM TURBINE DESIGN","Impulse vs reaction, stage efficiency, LP last stage, LNG plant"],[null,"10","PERFORMANCE CALC","Live Brayton and Rankine calculators, creep life, TBC delta-T"],[null,"11","REFERENCE TABLES","Superalloy properties, marine turbine data, steam tables, charts"],[null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"© 2026 Alper Alacam Naval Architecture . All rights reserved.",null,null]]}
