{"kind":"table","sheet":"COVER","address":"A1:D31","rows":31,"cols":4,"values":[[null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"NAVAL ARCHITECTURE",null,null],[null,"TEACHING TOOLKIT",null,null],[null,"VOLUME 20 :  Marine Auxiliary Systems",null,null],[null,"Power Generation, Boilers, Heat Exchangers, Pumps, Purifiers and Ship Services",null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"Alper Alacam  |  Naval Architect and Marine Engineer  |  Turkiye  |  2026",null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"ABOUT THIS VOLUME",null,null],[null,"The engineering support structure","The main engine gets the ship moving. The auxiliary systems keep everything alive. Without the auxiliary generators there is no electricity for navigation, communication, automation, or safety systems. Without the boilers there is no steam for fuel heating. Without the pumps there is no cooling water, no fuel supply, no ballast control. Without the purifiers the fuel and lubricating oil destroy the engine in days. Without the fresh water generator the crew has no drinking water after one week at sea. The marine engineer who understands all of these systems simultaneously is one of the most broadly educated engineers in the world.",null],[null,"Connection to earlier volumes","Vol.12: ship resistance gives the brake power P_B used in heat balance calculations. Vol.15: corrosion protection applies to seawater side of all heat exchangers. Vol.18: steam turbine thermodynamics connects to boiler steam conditions. Vol.19: main engine -- all auxiliary systems serve the main engine directly. The engine heat balance from Vol.19 is the starting point for exhaust gas boiler sizing and jacket water FWG production in this volume.",null],[null,"What this volume covers","Auxiliary generators: AC generation, power factor, load balance, generator sizing. Boilers: exhaust gas boiler heat recovery, oil-fired auxiliary boiler efficiency, steam demand calculation, boiler water treatment. Heat exchangers: LMTD method, effectiveness-NTU method, overall heat transfer coefficient, jacket water and lube oil cooler sizing. Pumps: centrifugal pump curves, system curves, NPSH, affinity laws, positive displacement pumps. Centrifugal purifiers: Stokes law, centrifugal settling velocity, separation factor, purifier vs clarifier. Fresh water generators: vacuum distillation, reverse osmosis, salinometer. Oily water separators: MARPOL Annex I 15 ppm, Stokes law settling velocity. Starting air: compressor work, two-stage optimum pressure, receiver capacity.",null],[null,"Primary references","Taylor D.A. (1996) Introduction to Marine Engineering 2nd ed. Butterworth-Heinemann. Woodyard D. (2009) Pounder's Marine Diesel Engines and Gas Turbines 9th ed. Cengel Y.A. and Boles M.A. (2014) Thermodynamics: An Engineering Approach 8th ed. McGraw-Hill. Cengel Y.A. and Cimbala J.M. (2014) Fluid Mechanics: Fundamentals and Applications 3rd ed. Incropera F.P. et al. (2011) Fundamentals of Heat and Mass Transfer 7th ed. Wiley. Alfa Laval (2020) Fuel and Lube Oil Purification. Alfa Laval AB. IMO (2011) MARPOL Annex I: Prevention of Pollution by Oil. ISO 8528 (2016) Reciprocating IC Engine Driven AC Generating Sets. Stokes G.G. (1851) Trans Cambridge Phil Society 9:8-106.",null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"WORKSHEET INDEX",null,null],[null,"No.","Sheet","Contents"],[null,"1","COVER","Introduction, connections to earlier volumes, references"],[null,"2","GENERATORS","AC generation, power factor, load balance, generator sizing"],[null,"3","BOILERS","EGB heat recovery, oil-fired boiler efficiency, steam demand"],[null,"4","HEAT EXCHANGERS","LMTD method, effectiveness-NTU, JW and LO cooler sizing"],[null,"5","PUMPS","Centrifugal curves, system curves, NPSH, affinity laws"],[null,"6","PURIFIERS","Stokes law, centrifugal separation, separation factor"],[null,"7","FWG","Vacuum distillation, reverse osmosis, production calculation"],[null,"8","OILY WATER SEP","MARPOL Annex I 15 ppm, Stokes settling velocity, OWS sizing"],[null,"9","STARTING AIR","Compressor work, two-stage optimum pressure, receiver capacity"],[null,"10","HEAT BALANCE","Engine heat balance, waste heat recovery, system integration"],[null,"11","REFERENCE TABLES","Load tables, fouling resistances, pump types, FWG comparison"],[null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null],[null,"© 2026 Alper Alacam Naval Architecture . All rights reserved.",null,null]]}
